1
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:10,560
A square garden has sides of X metres.

2
00:00:10,610 --> 00:00:14,990
The owner makes it 3 metres longer and 2 metres wider.

3
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:17,450
When X is 10, what is the new area?

4
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,100
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:23,680
The new sides are 13 and 12.

6
00:00:23,730 --> 00:00:26,710
13 times 12 is 156 square metres.

7
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:32,040
It is not X squared plus 6, which would only be 106.

8
00:00:32,090 --> 00:00:35,660
Remember: 4, bracket, X plus 3, is 4 X plus 12.

9
00:00:35,710 --> 00:00:40,060
And X, bracket, X minus 5, is X squared minus 5 X.

10
00:00:40,110 --> 00:00:44,750
Multiply every term in the first bracket by every term in the second.

11
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,190
A grid helps.

12
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:46,890
Your turn.

13
00:00:46,940 --> 00:00:50,230
Use the grid to expand X plus 3, times X plus 2.

14
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:53,510
Pause the video and try it.

15
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:57,750
Add the four parts: X squared, plus 3 X, plus 2 X, plus 6.

16
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:02,100
Collect the middle terms: X squared plus 5 X plus 6.

17
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:06,430
With X equals 10: 100 plus 50 plus 6 is 156.

18
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:09,350
That matches the garden.

19
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:14,480
A perfect square: X plus 4, all squared, is X plus 4 times X plus 4.

20
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:17,890
That gives X squared plus 8 X plus 16.

21
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:21,560
The difference of two squares: X plus A, times X minus A.

22
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:26,170
The middle terms cancel out, leaving X squared minus A squared.

23
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:27,550
Here is the method.

24
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:29,560
Step 1: draw a grid.

25
00:01:29,610 --> 00:01:33,980
Step 2: multiply each pair of terms, keeping the signs.

26
00:01:34,030 --> 00:01:36,230
Step 3: collect the like terms.

27
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:39,620
Usually these are the two middle terms.

28
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:43,010
Step 4: check by substituting a number.

29
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:45,810
Expand X minus 6, times X minus 2.

30
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:49,910
Negative 6 times negative 2 is positive 12.

31
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:54,660
Collect the middle terms: X squared minus 8 X plus 12.

32
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:55,400
Your turn.

33
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:57,820
Expand Y plus 5, times Y minus 5.

34
00:01:57,870 --> 00:02:00,830
Pause and work it out.

35
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:04,030
Y squared, minus 5 Y, plus 5 Y, minus 25.

36
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:05,900
The middle terms cancel.

37
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:09,020
The answer is Y squared minus 25.

38
00:02:09,070 --> 00:02:14,420
Use the difference of two squares to work out 41 times 39.

39
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:17,770
That is 40 plus 1, times 40 minus 1.

40
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:24,550
So it is 40 squared minus 1 squared: 1,600 minus 1, which is 1,599.

41
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,060
Zara expands X plus 3, all squared.

42
00:02:27,110 --> 00:02:29,040
Which line is wrong?

43
00:02:29,090 --> 00:02:30,160
Line 1 is wrong.

44
00:02:30,210 --> 00:02:34,300
She squared each term, and missed the middle terms.

45
00:02:34,350 --> 00:02:39,070
X plus 3, times X plus 3, is X squared plus 6 X plus 9.

46
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:42,590
Mental maths champions use this trick.

47
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:47,770
51 times 49 is 50 squared minus 1, which is 2,499.

48
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:49,150
One last question.

49
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:53,580
Use the difference of two squares to work out 31 times 29.

50
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:57,040
Pause the video and answer.

51
00:02:57,090 --> 00:03:02,210
31 times 29 is 30 plus 1, times 30 minus 1.

52
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:05,040
900 minus 1 is 899.

53
00:03:05,090 --> 00:03:08,870
To remember: multiply every term by every term.

54
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:13,650
X plus A, all squared, is X squared plus 2 A X plus A squared.

55
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:17,810
X plus A, times X minus A, is X squared minus A squared.

56
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:21,390
Collect like terms, and check with a number.

57
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:26,550
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.4 on Camday.
